	<!--
		Suppressions are accepted-with-tracking risks, not "make CI green" hacks.
		Each entry MUST include:
		  - notes: rationale + reachability assessment
		  - the precise CVE id list (one <cve> per CVE)
		  - a tightly scoped <packageUrl> or <filePath> matcher
		  - an `until` expiry; renew explicitly

		The build in `env-deploy` fails on CVSS >= 7 (HIGH/CRITICAL) for any
		non-suppressed finding. Suppress only after writing down WHY the issue
		does not (currently) translate into actual risk for our users.
	-->

	<!-- ============================================================
	     Vendored Mozilla NSS toolkit (certutil.windows.zip — sqlite3.dll only)
	     ============================================================
	     M3.4 (2026-05-07) repacked certutil.linux.zip and certutil.osx.zip with
	     current NSS (Debian 3.123 + Homebrew 3.123.1). Those bundles no longer
	     trigger any SQLite CVEs.

	     The Windows bundle still contains the 2010-era sqlite3.dll. Mozilla does
	     not publish standalone NSS Windows binaries, so the repack requires a
	     Firefox install on a Windows host (see scripts/repack-nss-windows.ps1).
	     This is tracked as M3.4-windows in the roadmap.

	     Reachability assessment for the remaining Windows sqlite3.dll CVEs:
	       - The DLL is invoked exclusively by certutil.exe, locally, against the
	         user's own NSS profile DB. There is no SQL surface exposed to network
	         input, attacker-controlled file, or remote untrusted data.
	       - Trigger conditions require a malicious SQL statement or a crafted
	         database. The configurator does neither: it only runs `certutil -A`
	         and `certutil -D` with fixed args.
	       - The configurator runs once at install / uninstall time, then the
	         binary is no longer executed.

	     Suppression scope: ONLY the sqlite3.dll inside certutil.windows.zip.
	     The other DLLs in the same archive are checked separately.

	     Reviewer: <name pending>, 2026-05-07.
	     Renews: 2026-12-31 (or earlier if M3.4-windows ships).
	-->
	<suppress until="2026-12-31Z">
		<notes><![CDATA[
			Windows-only: vendored sqlite3.dll inside certutil.windows.zip
			(2010-era NSS bundled with the configurator). Local-only invocation,
			no attacker-controlled SQL surface. M3.4-windows replaces this when
			a Windows host with Firefox is available. Linux/macOS bundles were
			repacked in M3.4 with current NSS and no longer hit these CVEs.
		]]></notes>
		<filePath regex="true">.*certutil\.windows\.zip([\\/]+certutil[\\/]+|: )sqlite3\.dll</filePath>
